node_modules/
.wrangler/
.dev.vars
dist/
coverage/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Scratch tests written by review/design subagents. `git add -A` has no
# opinion about intent: four such files reached commits on 2026-08-01, and
# test/zzRefuteScratch.test.ts sat on main from 07-28 with two tests and ZERO
# expect() calls — it could never fail, and it was counted green in every test
# total all three sessions quoted for four days. A test count is the evidence
# a change is safe; it must not include files nobody read.
#
# The patterns are a naming convention made unstageable, which is the cheap
# 90% and not a guarantee. Worth stating the hole rather than implying there
# isn't one: zzcoverage.probe.test.ts was caught only because the agent
# happened to prefix it, and a file named coverage.probe.test.ts would have
# walked straight through the guard written in response to it.
test/zz*
test/_scratch*
test/*.probe.test.ts
test/*.scratch.ts

# Duplicate-file artifacts: "<name> 2.ext" beside "<name>.ext". Local tooling
# produced these three times during one session (a stash/pop and two rebases),
# and 21 of them reached main in #134 through a `git add -A`. They are not
# harmless copies:
#   - `.github/workflows/thirteenf-backfill 2.yml` registers a SECOND workflow
#     on the same cron, so the 13F backfill would have run twice.
#   - a duplicate migration made readD1Migrations run CREATE TABLE filings_13f
#     twice, which broke local test collection outright.
#   - duplicate *.test.ts files re-run whole suites under a second name.
# Ignored rather than remembered, because every instance so far was noticed
# only after it had already been committed or had already broken something.
# Deliberately literal " 2." / " 3." and not a digit class: a pattern like
# "* [0-9].*" would also swallow a legitimate "Q1 2.md".
* 2.*
* 3.*

# Subagent/probe scratch files. D-12 recurred on 2026-08-06 when `git add -A`
# swept two of these into a commit; they are never repo content.
test/tmp-*
